{"id":"assistant-1da9ae87-8cb4-5d40-89cd-5afc95db8d34","sessionId":"09b651a3-f92e-427e-d2f3-3d48b743c26e","turnId":"turn-be9b7f2ed0553ed6bb0de830ba168f0e","inputEntryId":"user-turn-be9b7f2ed0553ed6bb0de830ba168f0e-1","createdAt":1794279688777,"updatedAt":1794279688777,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! The task is complete. Let me provide a summary:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the caching issue in the bot. Here's what was done:\n\n### The Problem\nEvery `save_fact` call was causing the entire system prompt (~1046-1104 tokens) to be re-cached because the static instructions and volatile athlete context were combined into a single cache-controlled block. When facts changed, the entire block's prefix hash changed, evicting everything from the cache.\n\n### The Solution\nModified `bot.py`'s `build_system` function to split the system prompt into **two separate cache-controlled blocks**:\n\n1. **Block 1**: Static `INSTRUCTIONS` (~780 tokens) - byte-identical across all users and days\n2. **Block 2**: Volatile `athlete_context(a, today)` (~240 tokens) - contains date, profile, zones, goal, facts, and language\n\nNow when `save_fact` modifies the athlete's facts, only the second block (~240 tokens) is re-cached, while the first block (~780 tokens) stays hot in the prompt cache.\n\n### Files Changed\n- **`bot.py`**: Modified the `build_system` function (lines 130-137)\n- **`ANSWER.md`**: Created to document the changes and which parts of the colleague's note applied\n\n### What Applied from the Colleague's Note\n- Split system into two text blocks with separate `cache_control` markers\n- Block 1 = static instructions (byte-stable)\n- Block 2 = volatile data (date, profile, memory/facts)\n- Memory writes now invalidate only the tail\n- Using 2 of the 4 allowed cache markers\n\n### Expected Impact\nReduces token cost of memory writes by ~75% (saving ~780 tokens per `save_fact` call). The usage logs should now show `cache_creation_input_tokens` ~240 and `cache_read_input_tokens` ~780 after a memory write, instead of the full ~1046 tokens being re-cached."}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
